{"path":"outputs/pr_review_comments/suggestion-duplicate-registrant-names.md","content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: registrant names are not uniqueness-checked — a same-named pair makes the E7 report ambiguous**

`HostExtension.name` is documented as the registrant id that "E7 collision reports name both sides", but nothing rejects two extensions declaring the same name. `_rejectToolIdCollisions` keys each group as `'extension "${wired.extension.name}"'`, so a collision between two same-named extensions renders as:

```
Tool-id collision at build time (E7): "yoclip_cut" is registered by
both extension "yoclip" and extension "yoclip" — ...
```

The tool id keeps the report actionable, but the registrant half is noise — exactly the field the constructor goes out of its way to make meaningful. Mirror the constructor's duplicate-tool-id check at wire time, e.g. in `wireAgentCore` before/inside `_wireExtensions`:

```dart
final names = <String>{};
for (final extension in services.extensions) {
  if (!names.add(extension.name)) {
    throw HostWiringException(
      'Duplicate extension registrant name "${extension.name}" — '
      'registrant ids must be unique (E7 names both sides).',
    );
  }
}
```

Fold-in nit: `name.trim().isEmpty` is validated, but the raw (possibly whitespace-padded) name is stored and echoed verbatim into every E6/E7 message — consider storing `name.trim()`.

Non-blocking: today the only in-repo declarer is `AgentCli` (`cli-plugins`), so no live path produces duplicates.
